		}
		{
			dependencies: ["647A9F38BEF74CD7"]
			description: [
				"&7[NCP Field Memo #3508: Colony]"
				""
				"One bee is a hobby. An &bexpansion box&r (eight oak planks round a honeycomb) on top of the advanced"
				"beehive takes it from 3 bees to &b5&r, and opens the upgrade slots (productivity, speed)."
				"&aMore bees:&r feed two grown honey bees a flower each and they breed. Honey eggs are also in the NCP Shop."
				"&bBee cages&r (a honey bottle between two planks, four at a time) carry a bee: right-click it to catch,"
				"right-click the ground to let it go."
				"&7Bees that work for you instead of for honey start further down: solitary nests and worker bees."
			]
			id: "3AE416EDEA558437"
			rewards: [
				{
					count: 3
					id: "19CF49697660EB11"
					item: "positronics:ncp_scrip"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "11AEABBCB80E3135"
					item: "productivebees:expansion_box_oak"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "More Bees"
			x: 10.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3AE416EDEA558437"]
			description: [
				"&7[NCP Field Memo #3509: Solitary]"
				""
				"Not every bee keeps a hive. &bSolitary bees&r live alone in a nest, make no honey and won't move into"
				"your beehive. What they're good for is &bbreeding&r: the right two make a worker bee."
				"A crafted nest is empty. Place it, right-click it with a &bhoney treat&r, and after a while a bee moves in."
				"Which bee depends on the nest:"
				"&bOak Nest&r (wooden sword, oak log): a Green Carpenter or a Yellow-Black Carpenter bee."
				"&bDirt Nest&r (wooden sword, coarse dirt): a Chocolate Mining, Ashy Mining or Leafcutter bee."
				"&bStone Nest&r (iron sword, stone): a Digger or a Mason bee."
				"&7Glass box rules still apply. A solitary bee is just as good at finding the void."
			]
			id: "4B900A3C1EF3FE40"
			rewards: [
				{
					count: 3
					id: "731C7C6C39152FDE"
					item: "positronics:ncp_scrip"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			tasks: [
